apt 2.7.14 apt-pkg: embed dpkg arch tables for OHOS (no /usr/share/dpkg)

pkgInitArchTupleMap() builds the architecture<->tuple map from dpkg's
cputable+tupletable.  On OHOS/musl /usr/share/dpkg does not exist, so the
map stays empty and all multiarch tuple matching breaks: apt-cache search
and the libapt test "any-arm"/"any-amd64"/"linux-any" patterns return
false, e.g.

  CacheFilterTest.ArchitectureSpecification:
    cachefilter_test.cc:82  ams("any-arm") actual false expected true
    cachefilter_test.cc:90  ams("armhf")   actual false expected true

Verified: /usr/share/dpkg/cputable does not exist on the OHOS host.

Fix: embed dpkg 1.21.x /usr/share/dpkg/{cputable,tupletable} data (fetched
from the dpkg 1.21.23 source) and use it when the files are absent, so
the tuple map matches a Debian system.  On Debian the files exist and the
normal file parsing path is taken; this branch is inert.
